{
 "result": "csvsum.py is a pure-Python single-pass reader: it reads stdin as bytes, splits lines, skips the header, parses cat and val per row, accumulates sums in a dict, then writes sorted \"cat,sum\" lines with 2 decimals. It passes the public sample (in-0 vs out-0 check reported PASS), and the harness accepted it as baseline 2.0598 with 1.2% noise. I'm stopping here rather than spending energy on a rewrite, since beating the baseline by more than 3% is uncertain and the thinking cost could exceed any likely gain.",
